menu "Conveyor Monitor Project Configuration"

    config MQTT_BROKER_URI
        string "MQTT broker URI"
        default "mqtt://raspberrypi.local:1883"
        help
            URI of the MQTT broker to connect to.

            Default assumes a Mosquitto broker running on the Raspberry Pi
            itself (see deploy/mosquitto/), reachable via the mDNS hostname
            Raspberry Pi OS advertises out of the box (avahi-daemon). If mDNS
            doesn't resolve on network (some hotspots/routers block it),
            replace with the Pi's LAN IP instead: mqtt://<pi's LAN IP>:1883


    config MPU6500_SDA_GPIO
        int "MPU6500 I2C SDA GPIO"
        default 21
        help
            GPIO connected to the MPU6500's SDA pin.

    config MPU6500_SCL_GPIO
        int "MPU6500 I2C SCL GPIO"
        default 22
        help
            GPIO connected to the MPU6500's SCL pin.

    config MPU6500_INT_GPIO
        int "MPU6500 INT GPIO"
        default 4
        help
            GPIO connected to the MPU6500's INT pin. The sensor pulses this
            line once per internal sample (DATA_RDY, enabled in
            mpu6500_enable_data_ready_interrupt()); app_main.c attaches a
            GPIO ISR here that wakes sample_task, so sampling is driven by
            the sensor's own hardware interrupt rather than a software
            timer.

    config MPU6500_I2C_FREQ_HZ
        int "MPU6500 I2C bus frequency (Hz)"
        default 400000
        help
            I2C clock speed used to talk to the MPU6500.

    config SAMPLE_RATE_HZ
        int "Accelerometer sample rate (Hz)"
        default 500
        range 4 1000
        help
            The single source of truth for the sample rate. mpu6500_init()
            programs the sensor's SMPLRT_DIV register from it
            (rate = 1kHz / (1 + SMPLRT_DIV) with the DLPF enabled), so it
            must evenly divide 1000: e.g. 1000, 500, 250, 200, 125, 100.
            Other values fail the build. Sampling is driven by the sensor's
            own DATA_RDY interrupt at this rate, and the value is sent as
            the JSON payload's sample_rate_hz field, which the backend uses
            for the FFT frequency axis. Keep it above twice the highest
            mechanical frequency of interest (Nyquist); note the accel DLPF
            cuts off at ~184Hz regardless.

    config SAMPLE_WINDOW_SIZE
        int "Samples per published window"
        default 256
        help
            Number of samples buffered per axis before publishing one MQTT
            window as JSON. A power of two is recommended because
            most FFT implementations are radix-2 and prefer it.

endmenu
